WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.910
Everyone, Kaleido Star is going to start.

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:06.880
When you watch Kaleido Star,
please keep your room brightly lit,

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.140
and sit as far from the TV as you can.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.910
Well, well, well.
What are you good at doing?

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.280
Cooking? Participating in sports?
Or studying?

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:21.320
Mia is very good at coming up with
storylines and writing.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.760
I'm so excited to find out what kind of
story she is going to write.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:27.720
Let's support hard working Mia.
Let's support! Let's support!

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.740
<i>Dare mo sagashiteru yume wa kitto aru</i>

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.740
<i>The dream everyone is looking for
must be someplace</i>

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.240
<i>Dokoka ni aru</i>

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.240
<i>It has to be somewhere</i>

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:45.940
<i>Negai ga itsuka kanau made hitori ja nai</i>

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:45.940
<i>Until your dream comes true someday,
you're not alone</i>

00:00:53.990 --> 00:01:00.300
<i>Saigo made yareru to ittetane</i>

00:00:53.990 --> 00:01:00.300
<i>Remember how I used to say
I could make it to the end?</i>

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:06.670
<i>Kitto tsuyogatte itanda</i>

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:06.670
<i>I must have been pretending to be tough</i>

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:15.380
<i>Itsudatte muchabakka de
zutto karamawari de</i>

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:15.380
<i>Everything I did was reckless
and it never got me anywhere</i>

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:21.910
<i>Dakedo anata dake ga soba ni ita</i>

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:21.910
<i>But you alone were always beside me</i>

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:28.620
<i>Daremo sagashiteru yume wa kitto aru</i>

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:28.620
<i>The dream everyone is looking for
must be somewhere</i>

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.230
<i>Aruki daseru</i>

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.230
<i>You can start going forward</i>

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:36.770
<i>Koko kara nani kaga hajimaru</i>

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:36.770
<i>From this moment, something will start</i>

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.800
<i>Shinjite itai</i>

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.800
<i>I want to believe that</i>

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:46.310
<i>Mada minu hikari yakusoku no
basho e to tsuzuite yuku</i>

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:46.310
<i>The light I haven't seen yet
is beaming toward the promised place</i>

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:56.780
<i>Negai ga itsuka kanau made hitori ja naisa</i>

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:56.780
<i>Until your dream comes true someday,
you're not alone</i>

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.120
One week...

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.220
Make it so you can perform this
on stage in one week.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.060
Yes!

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:11.370
Fire It Up! Amazing Mia

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.070
Fire It Up! Amazing Mia

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.070
"Fire It Up! Amazing Mia"

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:17.230
Fire It Up! Amazing Mia

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.700
As a first step, come up with a
tentative plan in three days.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.020
In three days...

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.140
Go, Mia!

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.550
Everyone's future is on your shoulders, Mia.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:35.790
Why do you have to pressure me like that?!

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.030
I'm trying hard, but I can't write!

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.050
Sorry...

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.050
I'm trying hard, but I can't write!

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.560
I have to write.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:50.340
Maybe this is impossible for me...

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.670
I don't think so.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:52.710
Not at all. Not at all. Not at all.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:53.540
You think so?

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.880
You're not good at working under pressure.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:56.750
That's right. That's right.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:00.320
You can't write because you're trying to
write a masterpiece from the very beginning.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.810
Be yourself. Be yourself.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.020
You're right.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.110
Maybe I'm a little too zealous.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:09.420
We also have to be careful that we
don't say anything unnecessary.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.620
Telling you how much we're expecting
from you is not a good idea.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:12.960
Okay, then.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.690
First, I think I should relax and...

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:17.460
Did you write that fantastic masterpiece yet?

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.500
I got so excited, I couldn't sleep,

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.840
so I brought you something to eat!

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:22.800
Huh?

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:24.700
Oh, dear...

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:27.800
It's not a laughing matter.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.940
Now, now, have a break.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:34.270
First of all, why does the Boss
want me to correct this?

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:38.040
I don't know what he wants from me when
he just says, "Not good. Correct it! "

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:41.790
Now you mention it,
he always just says "Do it! "

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:43.560
Even when we played The Little Mermaid,

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.790
he just told Sora to create her own
little mermaid at the beginning...

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.260
You're right.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:51.820
If he told her what needed to be done,
Sora wouldn't have suffered as much.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.340
What do you think, Miss Sarah?

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:55.540
What do I think?

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.030
Kalos has always been like that.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:01.640
Kalos has been like that since he
started Kaleido Stage.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:04.870
So, in those days, he used to revise
the contents of the performance everyday.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:09.010
So the contents of the show
were different every day.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:12.540
Since Kaleido Stage has grown so much,

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:16.420
performing exactly the same show
became ordinary.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:20.200
Still, the way how Kalos handles
everything has not changed.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.760
How?

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.530
Take your Little Mermaid, for example.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:27.340
If you based that character on what
someone told you to do, how would you feel?

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:30.600
Do you think you'd be as attached
to that character as you are now?

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.300
Well... It could be...

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:34.340
But, of course,

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.710
maybe he just doesn't want to
think of it himself.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:40.680
By the way,

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.510
do you already have a rough idea of
what kind of story you want to write?

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.050
Well, sort of...

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.720
Considering the number of people we have,

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:49.990
I'm thinking about writing
that ghost love story.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.760
But, in order to use it for stage,

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:54.430
I think something is still missing.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:55.900
Well...

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.530
You may find a hint in the
materials in this room.

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:02.740
Isn't this performance using the cloth pretty?

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.440
I want to try this.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.410
I wonder if I can do fire-breathing?

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.400
What? Even though you're a diva?

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.570
I wonder if I should try something
with a motorcycle.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:11.950
In the end,

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:15.970
I think the performance we can do
depends on who we have left.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:17.810
That's true.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:21.560
Does everyone really think that
Yuri's theatrical company is that great?

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:23.060
According to the rumor,

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:24.760
anyone who left Kaleido Stage

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.560
can join his theatrical company
unconditionally.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:28.820
Seriously?

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:31.170
You want to go?

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:35.670
Maybe we're too talented, and he's,
like, afraid of asking us to join.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:36.840
That's right.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:39.670
You know, I think he, like,
just forgot about you.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:40.470
How dare you!

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:44.440
Let's go, Mia! Go beyond Shakespeare!

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.040
Miss Sarah...

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:51.210
Since Mia is working hard,
I also have to work hard.

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:57.620
Kaleido Stage is not as great a place
as you think.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:01.160
Kalos has misled everyone.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.860
You look like you're having
a hard time sleeping.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:07.070
Are you worried about something?

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:07.930
Kind of...

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:12.000
Oh, you don't need to read Tarot.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:13.200
What?!

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:16.380
Besides, I know it will just
show something bad.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:17.240
Well...

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:20.010
Then, I will sing a lullaby for you.

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:21.040
What?!

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:23.990
Okay. Then,

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:29.760
Lalaru, larula, sleep, good girl.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.090
Larula, lalaru, go on and...

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:34.290
You sound creepy. I can't sleep!

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:34.290
Larula, lalaru, go on and...

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:35.630
Okay...

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.400
Oh, Mia. You woke up?

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:46.170
Where is Sora?

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.170
She came here first thing in the morning...

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.680
...and she went to the practice room.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:51.680
Really?

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:52.870
Something happened?

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:54.150
Yeah...

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:57.120
As of today, thirteen more people are leaving.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:58.680
Oh...

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.880
Sora... Is she crying?

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:09.230
Sora!

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:10.730
Sora!

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.230
Hang in there, Sora!

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:17.500
Thanks...

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:20.010
It's dangerous to try that by yourself.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:21.280
If you ask me,

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:22.440
I'll teach you how to do it properly.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:23.780
Okay.

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:26.450
Anyway, 13 more people are quitting.

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:27.280
What?

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.320
The way things are going now,

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.650
we will end up having a little over
ten people left with us.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:35.520
Simon!

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:37.390
Simon Park!

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:40.360
You were saying?

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.600
Please continue what you were saying.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:43.530
Yeah.

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:46.330
I already heard about Kaleido Stage's
situation through the grapevine.

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:47.870
And yet,

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:52.170
Kalos is ready to let an absolute amateur
take charge of the next performance.

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:53.510
Frankly, I'm disappointed in him.

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:56.000
That's why I'm asking you to do this.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.740
Okay, no problem.

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:59.410
Okay?

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:00.510
You accept that easily?

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:04.290
I've been interested in Kaleido Stage
for a long time.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:06.310
But, I don't know what
Kalos will say about this.

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:07.480
I will persuade him.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.190
What?

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:14.520
Well, I thought you're a pretty cool woman.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:17.300
Please listen to me seriously.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.390
I am listening.

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:23.370
After three days,
a tentative plan will be ready.

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:24.740
Once he sees that plan,

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:27.440
he has no choice but to acknowledge
what we have to say.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:32.340
Unless we do something,
Kaleido Stage will be finished.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:38.720
Yes.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:39.710
It's Naegino.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:41.820
Come in.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:43.690
Why don't you have a seat?

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:44.920
Yes.

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:49.090
I'm so happy that you came here to visit me.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:51.330
Well...

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.130
About that thing you were
talking about the other day...

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.170
Since I don't know what will happen
to Kaleido Stage,

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:58.810
I thought maybe I should just
cut all ties, clean and completely,

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:01.110
take care of everything
once and for all and join your place.

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:02.840
But then, I still can't decide
what I should do.

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:03.340
Your acting is terrible.

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:03.340
But then, I still can't decide
what I should do.

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:04.550
Your acting is terrible.

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:05.670
Oh...

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:07.240
I know you want to say something.

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:17.930
I want to know why you are trying
to destroy Kaleido Stage.

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:18.760
I want to find out why...

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:21.320
This is...

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:23.730
revenge!

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.000
Really?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.170
Yeah...

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.740
When did you find out about this?

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:31.870
Only a year ago.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.470
So, that's what's going on...

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:38.350
Yuri Killian is Arlon Brass' son.

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:40.310
It seems that Killian
is his mother's maiden name.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.320
Yuri is trying to take revenge on me.

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:44.790
That's right.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:47.590
I have been waiting for this day to come.

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:51.730
My father was a trapeze artist like me,

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:54.890
and he was also one of
Kaleido Stage's founders.

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.930
But Kalos killed him.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:58.830
What?!

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:08.980
Uh...

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:11.950
Sora, please come to my place.

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:16.150
We still don't have a female top star.

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:21.560
And you have enough qualification
to be one. I need you.

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:22.350
I...

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:31.070
In the end, only about ten people
are going to remain.

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:34.060
Yuri... I really can't forgive him.

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:36.270
Are you okay, Mia?

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:40.270
If this was when we had so many people...

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:40.880
Oh...

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:41.110
What?

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:41.110
Oh...

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:41.710
What?

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:45.880
How about if the leading character
of the ghost is the owner of a circus?

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:48.120
The protagonist became a ghost.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:51.310
He's alone, recalling a time
when the circus was cheerful.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:55.550
I know this story can give everyone
a chance to show off their best talents!

00:10:55.860 --> 00:11:00.660
And the only person left by his side
is the woman who was his lover.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:02.000
Yeah, yeah...

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.630
The last scene is a touching farewell.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:05.830
He says goodbye to the one
he loves the most

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:07.320
while he's lost in beautiful reminiscence.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:10.230
It'll make people cry.
I know it'll make people cry!

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:12.940
There is a chance that this could be an
amazing masterpiece.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:13.800
Go, Mia!

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:16.240
I may surpass Shakespeare!

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:17.140
Really?!

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.070
Finished!

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:38.230
Kalos,

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:41.300
as I expected, the things
I was worried about came true.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.400
After all, Mia is still an amateur.

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:48.240
With the help of Simon Park's direction,
let's re-create Cinderella.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.180
You don't have any objection,
don't you, Kalos?

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:53.640
What?

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:56.150
Mr. Simon Park is here.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:57.050
Let him in.

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:59.040
So, everything is set, right?

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:01.720
Mia, you can leave now.

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:04.080
Yes...

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:04.990
No...

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:09.390
The next show will be directed
and produced by Mia Guillem.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:11.560
Kalos!

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:13.600
Revise the script.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:15.230
You still have four days until the deadline.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:18.840
Then...

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.640
Let's just say we weren't
meant to work together this time.

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.300
We should do dinner some other time.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:24.510
Simon Park!

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:25.950
Please wait.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:28.950
I want you to be a supervisor.

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:31.820
I'd like to ask you to support Mia Guillem.

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:34.550
Kalos, I think that is so rude.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:39.620
No. It sounds interesting. I will do it.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.050
Oh...

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:44.100
Well, I have places to go,
so I have to excuse myself now.

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:45.900
Send the script to my address.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:48.270
As for everything else,
please talk to my agent.

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:49.670
Then, take care of the rest.

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:54.300
That Simon Park is going to support me?

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:57.610
All right.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:10.990
What?!

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:12.890
That is amazing!

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:13.900
Yeah, yeah.

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:19.530
Right? That genius, Simon Park,
is going to read my script.

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:21.260
That itself makes me so happy.

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:26.040
I will strive to revise any kinds
of correction to perfection.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.440
Yeah!

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:28.840
First of all,

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:30.440
I should revise the parts I don't like.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:31.380
Mia is making steady progress.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:31.380
I should revise the parts I don't like.

00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:33.380
Mia is making steady progress.

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:37.150
I shouldn't be feeling this way either.

00:13:37.150 --> 00:13:38.520
About Mr. Yuri...

00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:42.120
I think I should talk to the Boss
and make sure of the truth.

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:48.060
Oh, sorry.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:49.030
Me too.

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:50.300
Going out?

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:53.190
Oh, yes. Well...

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:54.930
Huh?

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:59.410
So Yuri said that...

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:00.200
Yes.

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:04.680
Kalos forced my father
to do a risky maneuver.

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:07.410
And he used my father's death for promotion.

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:11.850
It's true that investors at that time
hid Arlon's death.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:13.790
Which actually led to the
rumor spreading more

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:15.560
and the audience numbers increased.

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:18.090
But I will tell you this.

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:19.530
Arlon was the one who tried that
maneuver, by his own choice.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.030
Then, Mr. Yuri is...

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:25.230
In fact, Yuri also should know better.

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:27.200
No matter how much someone
forces a person,

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:30.860
if that person is afraid of doing that,
he never can jump.

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:34.800
But Kalos has been blaming himself
for what happened.

00:14:35.510 --> 00:14:38.970
That's why he is silent and just
watching what Yuri is doing.

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:42.250
This is something very hard to deal with.

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:44.550
You and your friends don't need to
worry about something like this.

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:47.250
Instead, you should only focus
on your performance.

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:48.390
Yes.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:51.460
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.690
Yes, hello...

00:14:56.130 --> 00:14:58.790
Yes, could you please wait for a second?

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:00.690
A call from Simon Park to Mia.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:01.870
What!

00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:03.340
Yes!

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:06.640
So, you want me to delete
from page 2 to page 4.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:11.250
Then, you want me to delete
from the middle of page 5...

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:14.620
...to page 24?

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:15.980
Yes.

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:18.280
Then, you want me to change the last scene?

00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:19.820
Excuse me,

00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:23.360
but that's the scene when the protagonist
and his lover say good-bye, and...

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:27.050
I know. But we see this kind of
last scene all the time.

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:30.290
To replace the sections where we deleted,
why don't we do something fun?

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:34.700
And come up with a few more
highlight scenes for the climax.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:35.270
Yes.

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:35.570
Then, take care...

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:35.570
Yes.

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:36.300
Then, take care...

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.010
Um...

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:39.670
Mia...

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:42.540
In short, I need to rewrite it all.

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:44.170
All of it?

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:47.710
I will go to apologize to the Boss.

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:48.740
What?

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:51.520
I will tell him,
"Sorry, but I cannot do this."

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:52.920
I'm sorry everyone.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:54.390
Wait, Mia!

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:57.590
Are you going to quit?

00:15:57.590 --> 00:16:01.030
Because, if I continue
and can't finish writing it,

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:03.460
I will end up troubling you all. So...

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:04.400
You can do it!

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:05.990
Don't say something so irresponsible!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:08.640
I think you can do it.

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:12.710
Because I know Kalos never asks something
of someone who is not capable of doing it.

00:16:12.710 --> 00:16:13.670
But...

00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:15.940
I want you to write it, Mia.

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:17.710
I don't want you to give in to the pressure.

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:20.750
Once you make up your mind saying
that you can't do it,

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:21.610
that will be the end of it.

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:25.190
When we did the Triple Illusion,

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:28.560
I thought "we'll never make it"
so many times.

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:31.490
And I even stepped down from the role once.

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:35.490
But you said,

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:39.660
I'd rather perfect it with Anna and Sora.

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:43.830
At that moment, I thought
I have to do this by all means.

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:47.470
I thought, by all means,
I'm going to perfect it.

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:49.670
That was why I could push myself.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:52.040
Mia, let's do this to the last.

00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:55.180
Don't give up...

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:57.150
and do it to the last.

00:16:57.150 --> 00:17:00.480
Don't give up...

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:04.220
Don't give up?

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.050
Don't give up!

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:15.040
A story about people who don't give up.
This could be a good one.

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.940
It's perfect for us.

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:21.540
The number of members decreased,
but Kaleido Stage still exists.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.210
If this show becomes successful,

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:25.780
some of the people who left
Kaleido Stage may come back.

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:26.880
That's right.

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:30.180
If I make this wish into a part of the story...

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:32.150
Yeah. I think I can do this.

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:33.780
I wonder if I can gather everyone now.

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:35.820
Okay.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:36.720
Right away.

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:39.890
So, since we don't have that many people,

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:42.330
each of you, please be ready to perform

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:46.630
at least three kinds of routines
from your repertoire.

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:49.140
Unless I know the story, I can't do it.

00:17:49.140 --> 00:17:51.710
The script is not finished yet.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:52.110
What?

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:53.040
Not yet...

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:53.040
What?

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:54.280
How can she...

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:56.000
Can you finish writing the script?

00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:58.540
I will finish it. Absolutely...

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:02.010
Then, everyone, let's start practicing.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:03.250
Yes.

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:06.390
Good. Wrap the cloth
tight around your body.

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.240
Yes.

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:25.730
Then, I will revise it
so it will go to that direction.

00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:30.580
B #5 light is okay.

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:35.280
Everyone is working to create
their own performances.

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:37.280
It seems we are back
to the way we used to be.

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:38.340
Yeah.

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:40.590
I'm not sure.

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.490
Don't you think you can still make it better?

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:44.420
Hey, take a look at this.

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:46.920
What do you think about this kind of swing?

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:50.100
It looks interesting.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:51.500
I also want to try it.

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:53.630
Sora...

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:54.460
Yes.

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:56.740
Out of everyone left in Kaleido Stage,

00:18:56.740 --> 00:19:00.040
the only person who is
capable to be my partner is you.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:02.400
Even if you say no,
I'm still making you my partner.

00:19:03.110 --> 00:19:04.040
Yes.

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:06.550
Hmm, it's almost perfect.

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:07.380
Yes!

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:10.780
Since we still have eight more hours,
we should do one more push.

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:12.080
Yes!

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:17.490
Let's make it so the whole cast's mood
builds up at once toward the last scene.

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:22.190
I know conveying that kind of build up to the
audience is Kaleido Stage's charm, isn't it?

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:24.390
I understand. I will try.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:25.800
Mia...

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:26.820
You think you can make it?

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:29.800
Ouch!

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:39.310
I have one favor to ask.

00:19:39.850 --> 00:19:40.810
Yes.

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:43.810
Shorten all female performers' skirts.

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:45.320
What?

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.680
Your script is perfect.

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:51.660
We will raise the curtain for
opening day one week from today.

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:53.850
Start rehearsal immediately.

00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:55.280
Let's go, Mia.

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:58.120
Yes. Thank you very much.

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:03.130
The stage is the world of fire and darkness.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:06.900
This is the story about two groups of
young people fighting in that world.

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:12.910
In that scene, I want you to
perform more wildly.

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:13.610
Oh...

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:15.650
but, maybe, it's okay the way
you're doing it right now.

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:17.890
Direct with confidence!

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:18.870
Yes.

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:25.630
Originally, they were friends
in the same group.

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:28.890
While young men fight each other,
they begin to change.

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:34.100
It seems the director
gets new ideas every day.

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:35.970
She's a sceneman's worst nightmare.

00:20:35.970 --> 00:20:37.810
Jean, you're so alive.

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:38.670
You too.

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:42.330
Anna, more speed!

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:46.310
Sora, move bigger!

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:50.920
I thought of a title.

00:20:50.920 --> 00:20:52.390
Yume, Kibou...

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:53.510
Those are Japanese.

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:56.620
I started studying Japanese recently.

00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:58.160
Not good enough.

00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:58.950
I agree.

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:06.720
Soon, they start thinking that they want
to live together the way they used to.

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:10.960
And then, their wish reached
everybody's heart.

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:13.410
They acknowledged and forgave each other,

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:16.670
and decided to cooperate
and live together once again.

00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:24.390
Amazing!

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:26.880
I can definitely feel the
excitement on the stage.

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:29.320
When they free themselves from fighting,

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:33.760
I think that's the time
they obtain real freedom.

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:36.290
That's why this story's title is:

00:21:37.030 --> 00:21:38.090
"Freedom! "

00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:43.430
YEAH!

00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:51.700
You did it, Mia!

00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:55.940
Everyone is enjoying it. I'm happy.

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:11.270
One day, I'm sure the day we can
hear this applause

00:22:11.270 --> 00:22:13.890
with everyone, even all the
former members, will come.

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:15.670
I'm sure...

00:22:20.310 --> 00:22:22.280
Next Kaleido Star

00:22:23.010 --> 00:22:24.840
Hey, apologize to everyone!

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:29.740
And so, Mia's direction was a
big, big, big success! Yet...

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:31.150
Because of Yuri's plot...

00:22:31.150 --> 00:22:33.640
Today is Kaleido Stage's last day...

00:22:33.890 --> 00:22:34.820
Miss Layla,

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:38.520
what on earth are we going to do now?
What on earth? What on earth?

00:22:38.930 --> 00:22:40.520
Next time on Kaleido Star,

00:22:40.690 --> 00:22:42.930
"Yuri's Amazing Trap"

00:22:42.930 --> 00:22:43.860
Yuri's Amazing Trap

00:22:42.930 --> 00:22:43.860
"Yuri's Amazing Trap"

00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:46.100
Yuri's Amazing Trap

00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:46.100
My wings are my dream
and on towards the sky...

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:48.070
Yuri's Amazing Trap

00:22:51.440 --> 00:23:04.280
<i>Boku wa koko ni iru
sora to michi no aida de mukai kaze</i>

00:22:51.440 --> 00:23:04.280
<i>I'm here between the sky and the roads,
and facing against the wind</i>

00:23:04.280 --> 00:23:18.130
<i>Soshite mae o muiteiru
Mou nido to kanashimi ga furanai youni to</i>

00:23:04.280 --> 00:23:18.130
<i>And I'm facing forward so the sorrow
doesn't rain down ever again</i>

00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:24.000
<i>Ano kabe o koete kokomade kitanda</i>

00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:24.000
<i>I came all the way here after
I jumped over that wall</i>

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:31.210
<i>Nigedashitaku naru koto wa nando mo aru</i>

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:31.210
<i>There are many times
when I just want to run away</i>

00:23:31.210 --> 00:23:36.680
<i>Dakedo kokoni irunara taishite bibitte inai</i>

00:23:31.210 --> 00:23:36.680
<i>But I'm still here,
so, I'm not daunted that much</i>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:44.120
<i>Kakinaguri no uta "hajimekara yareba iisa"</i>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:44.120
<i>The poem I scribbled down, I can just
start writing over from the beginning</i>

00:23:44.120 --> 00:23:49.760
<i>Umaku kakenaku te boku wa waratte iru</i>

00:23:44.120 --> 00:23:49.760
<i>Unable to write it well, I'm laughing</i>
